The attached image from Figure 2 of the provided PDF illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image (Panel A) shows the spherical shape and irregular, "cauliflower-like" surface of the nanoparticles. The accompanying histogram (Panel B) details their size distribution, determined by dynamic light scattering, indicating a relatively uniform diameter predominantly between 75 and 80 nm. This size range is considered optimal for efficient uptake by dendritic cells, a key factor in Nano-11's effectiveness as a vaccine adjuvant.